Just completed the game ;
- A good story telling game, slow pace, no run and gun, atmosphere is great and the soundtracks too. Sometimes peacefull sometimes you are sitting on the edge of your chair. Take your time when playing it, would buy another game if the developer makes another one, its a different perspective among other survival genre. Regards with the "walking simulator" hates, well you are not non stop running in real life so take it easy.
Would recommend this game if the above suits you.

PROS: Superb X-ray shot system; a lot of ways to play missions (though the game is recommending stealthy approach); very good sound design; variety in mission objectives and locations;
CONS: buggy (enemies hearing you through muffling sounds, seeing you through obstacles, character gets stuck in cover mode; in a lot of places cover mode doesn't even work); campaign is quite short; story is meh
OVERALL: Not the best TPS around, but definitely better than other sniper games (yes, I'm looking at you, Ghost Warrior). Even though the game can be an ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ to the player, the satisfaction from well aimed 200m headshot (and seeing it all in X-ray) is recompensating all flaws.

